<title>GREECE: TABLE-Greek/Bund gap shrinks to 400bps, 320 vs BTP.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Greek/Bund gap shrinks to 400bps, 320 vs BTP.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A minor rally pushed the yield spread of Greek 10-year bonds over bunds down to 400 basis points from 417 bps following the central bank's 30 basis point cut in its intervention rate on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Greek/BTP gap narrowed to 320 basis points from 335 on Thursday.</p>
<p>		 CPN     MATURITY  YIELDS    SPREADS    PREVIOUS</p>
<p>								    SPREADS</p>
<p>   GREECE    8.80%   25JUN07    9.58%</p>
<p>   GERMANY   6.0%    04JUL07    5.58%	400	417 bps</p>
<p>   FRANCE    5.5%    25APR07    5.42%	416	433 bps</p>
<p>   ITALY     6.75%   01FEB07    6.38%	320	335 bps</p>
<p>   PORTUGAL  6.63%   23FEB07    6.27%	331	347 bps</p>
<p>   SPAIN     7.35%   31MAR07    6.20%	338	356 bps</p>
<p>   UK	  7.25%   07DEC07    7.10%	248	263 bps</p>
<p>   US	  6.63%   15MAY07    6.26%	332	344 bps</p>
<p>All yields are annualised and based on bid prices at 0905 GMT.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
